0009EA  1               ;CONTROl looks up a keyboard command in the list
0009EA  1               ;of control codes at CTBL. The first .byte of
0009EA  1               ;CTBL is the actual number of commands. Once the
0009EA  1               ;position is found, this position is doubled as
0009EA  1               ;an index to the two-byte address table at VECT.
0009EA  1               ;The address of MAIN-1 is put on the stack,
0009EA  1               ;simulating the return address; then the address
0009EA  1               ;of the command routine taken from VECT is pushed.
0009EA  1               ;We then perform an RTS. RTS pulls the .bytes off
0009EA  1               ;the stack as if they were put there by a JSR.
0009EA  1               ;This powerful technique is used to simulate
0009EA  1               ;ON+GOTO in machine language.
0009EA  1               CONTROL:
0009EA  1  8A                   TXA
0009EB  1  AE 0C 0A             LDX     CTBL
0009EE  1               SRCH:
0009EE  1  DD 0C 0A             CMP     CTBL,X
0009F1  1  F0 06                BEQ     FOUND
0009F3  1  CA                   DEX
0009F4  1  D0 F8                BNE     SRCH
0009F6  1  4C 49 09             JMP     main
0009F9  1               FOUND:
0009F9  1  CA                   DEX
0009FA  1  8A                   TXA
0009FB  1  0A                   ASL
0009FC  1  AA                   TAX
0009FD  1  A9 09                LDA     #>(main-1)
0009FF  1  48                   PHA
000A00  1  A9 48                LDA     #<(main-1)
000A02  1  48                   PHA
000A03  1  BD 35 0A             LDA     VECT+1,X
000A06  1  48                   PHA
000A07  1  BD 34 0A             LDA     VECT,X
000A0A  1  48                   PHA
000A0B  1  60                   RTS
000A0C  1               CTBL:
