00144D  2               
00144D  2               ;refresh copies a screenful of text
00144D  2               ;from the area of memory pointed to by
00144D  2               ;toplin. It works like a printer routine,
00144D  2               ;fitting a line of text between the screen
00144D  2               ;margins, wrapping words, and restarts
00144D  2               ;at the left margin after printing a car-
00144D  2               ;riage return. SpeedScript constantly calls
00144D  2               ;this routine while the cursor is blink-
00144D  2               ;ing, so it has to be very fast. To elimi-
00144D  2               ;nate flicker, it also clears out the end of
00144D  2               ;each line instead of first clearing the
00144D  2               ;screen. It stores the length of the first
00144D  2               ;screen line for the sake of the check
00144D  2               ;routine (which scrolls up by adding
00144D  2               ;that length to toplin), the last text
00144D  2               ;location referenced (so check can see
00144D  2               ;if the cursor has moved off the visible
00144D  2               ;screen).
00144D  2               
00144D  2               
